WEBVTT

00:01:30.230 --> 00:01:34.990
<b>Magical Girl - Another and Another</b>

00:01:35.440 --> 00:01:37.820
Hey, everyone who made it out today!

00:01:38.180 --> 00:01:42.330
My partner Michiru and I are 
gonna keep doing our best!

00:01:42.700 --> 00:01:45.320
We hope you'll keep supporting PRISMA!

00:01:45.780 --> 00:01:49.300
Thank you so much for coming today!

00:01:55.550 --> 00:01:58.840
<b>Okawa Michiru-sama
Kiryu Ruka-sama</b>

00:01:56.310 --> 00:01:58.840
Why did our audience shrink again?!

00:01:58.840 --> 00:02:00.090
It's impossible!

00:01:58.840 --> 00:02:03.350
<b>Deadline</b>

00:02:00.090 --> 00:02:01.930
It's gotta be the weather, right?

00:02:01.930 --> 00:02:03.340
There! Mystery solved.

00:02:03.650 --> 00:02:08.100
Our agency is still nagging us about 
our reduced attendance, though.

00:02:08.100 --> 00:02:09.860
We're getting pressure from below, too.

00:02:09.860 --> 00:02:13.020
Humph! I don't hear them.

00:02:13.450 --> 00:02:14.900
Micchi, you're so positive.

00:02:15.620 --> 00:02:18.670
I hate giving up on the stuff I do!

00:02:20.140 --> 00:02:23.250
Did you hear they canceled our next concert?

00:02:23.250 --> 00:02:25.210
Huh? What the hell?

00:02:25.210 --> 00:02:28.860
They said they wanted to match the timing 
to the release of our new song, but...

00:02:28.860 --> 00:02:30.360
What a crock!

00:02:30.360 --> 00:02:31.560
Yeah...

00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:37.060
If we held one big retirement event, 
we could make enough money

00:02:37.060 --> 00:02:39.140
to support ourselves for a while, right?

00:02:39.580 --> 00:02:41.960
Don't say that! It's depressing.

00:02:41.960 --> 00:02:43.370
I'm an idol!

00:02:43.370 --> 00:02:46.910
No matter what anyone says, 
I'm totally an idol for life!

00:02:47.560 --> 00:02:50.970
That's right. Michiru, you are an idol.

00:02:50.980 --> 00:02:53.230
<b>Guerilla Performance at 
Magical Girls Meet-and-Greet</b>

00:02:56.660 --> 00:02:58.690
You don't have to get so mad...

00:02:58.690 --> 00:03:00.410
It was a <i>group</i> meet-and-greet,

00:03:00.410 --> 00:03:03.160
but they still got all the spotlight!

00:03:03.160 --> 00:03:07.080
Well, you can do what you want 
when you're on the rise.

00:03:07.080 --> 00:03:09.020
And you're just okay with that?

00:03:09.020 --> 00:03:11.860
We did the same thing, remember?

00:03:13.360 --> 00:03:14.680
Remembering it?

00:03:15.380 --> 00:03:18.170
We were allowed because we had talent!

00:03:25.530 --> 00:03:29.130
No, no, no! He's my enemy! 
My professional rival!

00:03:29.130 --> 00:03:31.110
Who cares about him?

00:03:31.810 --> 00:03:33.190
Previously

00:03:33.810 --> 00:03:36.360
<i>We've realized that Hyoe is suspect.</i>

00:03:37.020 --> 00:03:42.370
<i>So we've decided to see what Hyoe 
and Mohiro-chan get up to all day.</i>

00:03:46.420 --> 00:03:47.690
Isn't this stalk—

00:03:47.690 --> 00:03:49.820
Hold it! This is an investigation!

00:03:49.820 --> 00:03:51.540
There's no ulterior motive!

00:03:51.540 --> 00:03:52.610
I didn't even fini—

00:03:52.610 --> 00:03:53.870
Don't finish!

00:03:54.800 --> 00:03:57.120
He showed up around 
Mohiro-chan out of the blue.

00:03:57.450 --> 00:04:00.120
He became friends with 
Mohiro-chan out of the blue.

00:04:00.540 --> 00:04:03.920
Then he dragged Mohiro-chan into the 
entertainment industry out of the blue!

00:04:04.690 --> 00:04:07.140
There's his "mystery man" attitude,

00:04:07.140 --> 00:04:11.590
and the way he tends to go missing 
at the most crucial times...

00:04:12.040 --> 00:04:14.840
And then there's the way he clings to him!

00:04:14.840 --> 00:04:16.910
Hey, Mohiro! Look at that!

00:04:17.020 --> 00:04:21.860
Oh!

00:04:18.500 --> 00:04:21.690
He's suspicious! Too suspicious! Dammit!

00:04:20.860 --> 00:04:21.860
Now, now...

00:04:22.610 --> 00:04:27.580
But he would know Nii-san's schedule.

00:04:30.740 --> 00:04:34.710
They seem to just be... shopping.

00:04:34.710 --> 00:04:37.090
No, we don't know that for sure yet.

00:04:37.500 --> 00:04:41.150
He might be planning to lead him 
somewhere and steal him away!

00:04:41.490 --> 00:04:43.710
We can't let our guard down yet!

00:04:44.610 --> 00:04:46.550
What are you doing?

00:04:46.550 --> 00:04:48.480
It's camouflage. Camouflage.

00:04:49.040 --> 00:04:53.460
Anyway, if Hyoe-san is behind this, 
what are we going to do about it?

00:04:54.470 --> 00:04:55.780
This!

00:04:55.780 --> 00:04:58.960
Pull out his heart and crush 
it in front of everyone?

00:04:59.700 --> 00:05:03.080
No... I was thinking more 
like a punch to the gut.

00:05:03.080 --> 00:05:05.610
Why did you take this to a murdery place?

00:05:11.180 --> 00:05:16.900
Well, if we just keep watching, he'll 
reveal his evil colors sooner or later.

00:05:16.900 --> 00:05:17.740
Yes?

00:05:18.350 --> 00:05:19.330
What? Now?

00:05:19.770 --> 00:05:20.990
Very well.

00:05:20.990 --> 00:05:22.260
Saki, let's go.

00:05:22.260 --> 00:05:23.970
Where to?

00:05:23.970 --> 00:05:25.070
We got a call.

00:05:25.390 --> 00:05:27.810
Konamin wants to meet us at 
the nearby family restaurant.

00:05:27.960 --> 00:05:31.480
Huh?! But we were just getting started!

00:05:36.380 --> 00:05:40.390
Quiz: How many years have 
we known each other now?

00:05:40.390 --> 00:05:43.290
Dunno. 500 million or so?

00:05:43.290 --> 00:05:45.620
Sorry, the answer is five years.

00:05:45.620 --> 00:05:48.700
A lot has changed. 
And a lot hasn't, I guess.

00:05:48.700 --> 00:05:50.070
What does that mean?

00:05:51.520 --> 00:05:54.350
Man, I wish we could 
become magical girls, too.

00:05:54.350 --> 00:05:56.800
It's not gonna be that easy.

00:05:56.800 --> 00:05:58.420
We'd just be copycats, anyway.

00:05:58.710 --> 00:06:02.900
But a copycat can catch up 
with or outpace the original.

00:06:03.670 --> 00:06:05.070
This is no laughing matter!

00:06:05.070 --> 00:06:06.290
Excuse me.

00:06:06.290 --> 00:06:07.720
Could I have a minute?

00:06:07.720 --> 00:06:09.120
No, you may not.

00:06:09.120 --> 00:06:11.570
I haven't said anything.

00:06:11.570 --> 00:06:15.200
Oh, I get it. I'm too much man for you?

00:06:15.200 --> 00:06:16.690
Whatever it is, we're not in the market.

00:06:17.260 --> 00:06:19.380
Hey, don't treat me like a cheap salesman.

00:06:19.380 --> 00:06:22.320
<i>Uh, but that's completely 
what you look like.</i>

00:06:22.630 --> 00:06:25.510
I've come with an amazing job offer.

00:06:25.510 --> 00:06:28.930
We're already signed with an agency.

00:06:28.930 --> 00:06:30.670
I give great rates.

00:06:30.670 --> 00:06:33.440
We don't do red light district gigs.

00:06:33.810 --> 00:06:34.730
No, no.

00:06:34.730 --> 00:06:37.380
I'm scouting for magical girls.

00:06:38.590 --> 00:06:42.060
So, are you interested in 
becoming magical girls?

00:06:43.380 --> 00:06:44.920
<b>Magical World
Magical Girl Mascot Department
Happy-chan</b>

00:06:44.920 --> 00:06:48.080
You're gonna be busy from now on.

00:06:48.080 --> 00:06:50.440
The magical girl industry 
is in the middle of an

00:06:50.440 --> 00:06:52.570
unprecedented generational 
changeover season.

00:06:52.570 --> 00:06:55.750
People from the last generation 
are retiring en masse,

00:06:55.750 --> 00:06:57.300
and there's a whole lot of openings.

00:06:57.820 --> 00:07:02.180
Recouping our numbers isn't 
as easy as it sounds, though.

00:07:02.180 --> 00:07:07.140
Not everyone is born with the ability
to become a magical girl.

00:07:07.670 --> 00:07:10.810
You two are chosen.

00:07:10.820 --> 00:07:19.460
<b>Sparkle</b>

00:07:11.800 --> 00:07:13.380
<i>No way!</i>

00:07:13.380 --> 00:07:15.330
<i>Are you falling for that, Michiru?</i>

00:07:15.330 --> 00:07:16.910
<i>You're so naive. So simple.</i>

00:07:16.910 --> 00:07:18.750
<i>So super-duper cute.</i>

00:07:19.440 --> 00:07:21.260
So, let me say this first.

00:07:21.260 --> 00:07:23.280
This lady here has what it takes,

00:07:23.280 --> 00:07:27.160
but this one is a little lacking 
in the magical girl component.

00:07:27.160 --> 00:07:28.700
And what component is that?

00:07:28.990 --> 00:07:30.910
Love Power.

00:07:30.910 --> 00:07:32.740
Love Power?

00:07:32.740 --> 00:07:34.110
Yeah, love!

00:07:34.110 --> 00:07:35.860
Romantic feelings for someone else.

00:07:35.860 --> 00:07:36.820
And I don't have enough?!

00:07:36.820 --> 00:07:38.720
But I'm the girliest girl there is!

00:07:38.720 --> 00:07:40.270
It's Ruka who's lacking there!

00:07:39.780 --> 00:07:42.090
I feel like I've been hit by friendly fire.

00:07:40.270 --> 00:07:43.840
Right? Right? Where is it? Right? Right?

00:07:42.390 --> 00:07:43.990
Now, now.

00:07:43.990 --> 00:07:47.020
We have a new special campaign 
package in the works,

00:07:47.020 --> 00:07:49.270
and you definitely qualify for that!

00:07:50.410 --> 00:07:53.390
We're signed to an agency. 
We can't take gigs.

00:07:53.390 --> 00:07:57.660
It's a different field, so don't you worry!

00:07:58.090 --> 00:08:01.450
Why not sign using a company name, then?

00:08:01.800 --> 00:08:04.630
That makes it easier to 
work out payment, too.

00:08:06.160 --> 00:08:08.640
Maybe that's better, then?

00:08:09.810 --> 00:08:12.250
Now, just write your names.

00:08:12.250 --> 00:08:14.480
It's provisional. This is all provisional.

00:08:14.480 --> 00:08:16.300
Of course, it's fine if you don't want to...

00:08:16.300 --> 00:08:18.000
Just sign your names.

00:08:19.150 --> 00:08:21.570
Is this about the event from before?

00:08:21.570 --> 00:08:23.460
Is everything all right?

00:08:24.900 --> 00:08:27.900
I entered that room, and it 
wasn't just my own bosses,

00:08:27.900 --> 00:08:30.060
but bigwigs from other agencies...

00:08:30.060 --> 00:08:33.660
even advisers from other entertainment 
industries were there...

00:08:34.080 --> 00:08:35.820
I was so scared...

00:08:37.980 --> 00:08:39.660
Aw, just teasin'!

00:08:39.660 --> 00:08:42.200
<b>Magical Girl Event</b>

00:08:39.660 --> 00:08:42.200
<b>Huge Panic</b>

00:08:39.660 --> 00:08:44.150
They were a little mad that we 
broke the day's event schedule,

00:08:42.200 --> 00:08:45.250
The magical girl meet-and-greet came with a show

00:08:44.150 --> 00:08:49.340
but we're in every paper, on TV, with 
pictures and videos on the web...

00:08:45.250 --> 00:08:48.130
<b>Breaking: Idol Meet-and-Greet Event Canceled</b>

00:08:48.130 --> 00:08:51.420
<b>Idol Event
Magical Girls</b>

00:08:49.340 --> 00:08:51.420
It was the best publicity imaginable!

00:08:52.030 --> 00:08:53.400
Okay, but...

00:08:53.400 --> 00:08:54.920
Is that all right?

00:08:54.920 --> 00:08:56.600
It's viral, you know?

00:08:56.600 --> 00:08:59.500
If it makes people happy, 
what's the problem?

00:08:59.500 --> 00:09:00.980
What a world.

00:09:01.590 --> 00:09:03.930
It's what makes the world go 'round.

00:09:04.140 --> 00:09:09.060
<b>Joint Concert</b>

00:09:04.140 --> 00:09:09.060
An Innovative 
Project

00:09:04.450 --> 00:09:06.560
And we arranged something else...

00:09:06.560 --> 00:09:08.420
A joint concert!

00:09:09.060 --> 00:09:12.400
Mikage Mohiro   Hyoe

00:09:09.470 --> 00:09:11.210
The boys will be with you.

00:09:11.210 --> 00:09:13.020
and PRISMA-san, too.

00:09:12.110 --> 00:09:16.450
<b>Ogawa Michiru  Kiryu Ruka</b>

00:09:13.020 --> 00:09:16.460
All right! I get to hear PRISMA sing live!

00:09:16.460 --> 00:09:18.480
Huh? You like them?

00:09:18.480 --> 00:09:21.550
All girls want to be them!

00:09:21.550 --> 00:09:23.840
I have a few of their CDs, even!

00:09:24.130 --> 00:09:26.620
Still, I'm impressed you 
managed to land the venue.

00:09:26.620 --> 00:09:28.060
Oh, that?

00:09:26.620 --> 00:09:53.220
<b>Johnson</b>

00:09:28.060 --> 00:09:31.700
PRISMA-san reserved it about a year ago,

00:09:31.700 --> 00:09:34.160
but then they weren't sure
 if they'd fill the seats,

00:09:34.160 --> 00:09:36.630
and were thinking they should cancel.

00:09:37.170 --> 00:09:39.090
R-Really?

00:09:39.090 --> 00:09:40.370
That's quite harsh...

00:09:40.700 --> 00:09:43.910
But with us there too, there's no issue!

00:09:43.910 --> 00:09:45.470
No problem!

00:09:45.470 --> 00:09:47.860
You sound very confident, but...

00:09:47.860 --> 00:09:51.030
You need to stop being so self-effacing.

00:09:51.030 --> 00:09:55.490
Besides, bringing excitement and smiles to the 
world isn't all being a magical girl is about.

00:09:55.490 --> 00:09:56.700
That's right.

00:09:56.700 --> 00:10:00.690
If we can bring our song 
to even more people...

00:10:01.070 --> 00:10:02.410
Yeah, yeah!

00:10:02.410 --> 00:10:03.740
That's right!

00:10:03.740 --> 00:10:05.040
That <i>is</i> right.

00:10:05.530 --> 00:10:09.950
Let's get you looking cool in 
front of a cheering crowd!

00:10:10.510 --> 00:10:11.410
Okay!

00:10:12.810 --> 00:10:16.450
Okay, once it's all official, 
I'll be in touch.

00:10:16.780 --> 00:10:21.160
There's a lot of fine print in those contracts, 
so make sure you read 'em through.

00:10:21.160 --> 00:10:22.460
O-Okay!

00:10:22.470 --> 00:10:23.760
Okawa Michiru

00:10:23.760 --> 00:10:24.970
Kiryu Ruka

00:10:45.670 --> 00:10:46.580
Oh, that?

00:10:46.580 --> 00:10:52.820
<b>Johnson</b>

00:10:46.920 --> 00:10:50.560
PRISMA-san reserved it about a year ago,

00:10:50.560 --> 00:10:52.830
but then they weren't sure
 if they'd fill the seats,

00:10:52.830 --> 00:10:55.580
and were thinking they should cancel.

00:10:57.460 --> 00:10:58.920
<b>Don't Fall in Love With My Lips</b>

00:11:05.000 --> 00:11:08.140
What'll we do? I put my name on it, but...

00:11:08.140 --> 00:11:11.490
I got so carried away I even stamped it.

00:11:11.940 --> 00:11:13.140
But now...

00:11:13.430 --> 00:11:15.930
If we can get the same 
popularity that they have...

00:11:13.430 --> 00:11:16.740
If I can tell if he feels 
the same way I do...

00:11:18.470 --> 00:11:20.900
I d-didn't say anything!

00:11:20.900 --> 00:11:23.780
<b>Humph!</b>

00:11:23.320 --> 00:11:28.690
<b>You dummy...</b>

00:11:23.420 --> 00:11:26.180
<i>Do people still act that 
transparent these days?</i>

00:11:26.180 --> 00:11:29.790
<i>It's so obvious! It's the 
cutest in the world!</i>

00:11:28.690 --> 00:11:29.780
<b>Hah... hah...</b>

00:11:30.610 --> 00:11:31.620
No!

00:11:36.950 --> 00:11:39.180
No one's comin' to save you!

00:11:42.110 --> 00:11:46.520
The fallen angels with severed 
wings now seek rebirth.

00:11:46.990 --> 00:11:49.280
Um...

00:11:49.280 --> 00:11:54.110
the principalities survive their 
jihad and arrive in Elysium.

00:11:54.730 --> 00:11:57.920
The ritual of revival... open the gate!

00:11:57.920 --> 00:12:00.900
PRISMA has arrived!

00:12:00.900 --> 00:12:03.000
We nailed it!

00:12:03.000 --> 00:12:06.640
I saw you thinking hard yesterday...

00:12:06.640 --> 00:12:09.630
Were you seriously thinking 
about this all night?

00:12:09.630 --> 00:12:13.560
So we'd stand out! That's the most 
important thing for any magical girl!

00:12:20.300 --> 00:12:23.460
We are PRISMA! Pleased to 
make your acquaintance!

00:12:23.900 --> 00:12:26.230
Thank you very much!

00:12:26.230 --> 00:12:28.760
Please post about us online!

00:12:29.460 --> 00:12:30.970
Hiya!

00:12:31.450 --> 00:12:34.220
What's with that form? Creepy.

00:12:34.220 --> 00:12:35.710
It's not creepy.

00:12:35.710 --> 00:12:40.180
Happy-chan, isn't there 
another way for us to fight?

00:12:40.180 --> 00:12:45.780
If we just let crooks bleed to death, it's 
no different from a delinquent manga.

00:12:45.780 --> 00:12:47.930
That's the way it's always been.

00:12:48.310 --> 00:12:52.370
I'd assumed magical girls would 
get to... you know, use magic.

00:12:52.370 --> 00:12:55.570
They've been working harder 
than we ever knew, I guess.

00:12:55.570 --> 00:12:57.100
Who are you thinking about?

00:12:57.480 --> 00:12:59.930
N-No one, okay?!

00:13:00.630 --> 00:13:03.330
<i>You're obviously thinking about someone!</i>

00:13:03.330 --> 00:13:06.210
<i>You dummy! You're the cutest ever!</i>

00:13:19.770 --> 00:13:22.630
Darn it! Why aren't we making the news?

00:13:22.630 --> 00:13:25.020
Come on, humanity, talk about me!

00:13:25.020 --> 00:13:26.770
What are you grinning about?

00:13:26.770 --> 00:13:29.160
Nothing like that.

00:13:29.770 --> 00:13:34.420
A new magical unit operating 
behind the scenes?

00:13:33.790 --> 00:13:41.670
<b>A new magical unit operating 
behind the scenes?</b>

00:13:34.420 --> 00:13:37.180
No need to rush things. It's coming, slowly.

00:13:37.790 --> 00:13:41.680
But I don't seem to have much time left...

00:13:42.610 --> 00:13:43.900
You noticed, huh?

00:13:43.900 --> 00:13:45.300
Of course I did!

00:13:45.300 --> 00:13:48.600
Hey, why is that?! Why am I 
the only one getting old, here?!

00:13:48.600 --> 00:13:51.190
Why do you still look the same? Why?!

00:13:48.810 --> 00:13:53.280
<i>But your older male form 
is still hot as hell!</i>

00:13:51.190 --> 00:13:56.580
How is anyone gonna accept 
me as a cute idol like this?!

00:13:57.300 --> 00:13:59.840
Well, maybe it's a disposition thing?

00:13:59.840 --> 00:14:02.660
You might not be cut out 
to be a magical girl.

00:14:03.290 --> 00:14:05.070
What this? What's up?

00:14:05.070 --> 00:14:06.720
What do you mean, "what's up"?!

00:14:06.720 --> 00:14:08.570
Explain all this!

00:14:08.870 --> 00:14:10.590
Oh, oh, oh?

00:14:10.590 --> 00:14:12.320
You read the contract, didn't you?

00:14:12.700 --> 00:14:13.890
Look, this part here.

00:14:13.890 --> 00:14:15.720
Super fine print...

00:14:15.720 --> 00:14:20.940
You signed up for our special 
campaign package, Michiru-san.

00:14:20.940 --> 00:14:23.790
The Double Love Power package.

00:14:23.790 --> 00:14:28.250
It lets you transform with 
half the usual Love Power,

00:14:28.250 --> 00:14:31.670
but in exchange, your 
magical girl lifespan is....

00:14:31.670 --> 00:14:32.690
My lifespan is...

00:14:32.970 --> 00:14:34.930
It's a teeny bit shorter.

00:14:34.930 --> 00:14:36.320
What the heck?!

00:14:36.320 --> 00:14:37.700
What do you expect?

00:14:37.700 --> 00:14:40.150
You just didn't have enough Love Power!

00:14:40.150 --> 00:14:42.680
I don't like it! I don't like it!

00:14:42.680 --> 00:14:45.290
I quit! I quit being a magical girl!

00:14:45.290 --> 00:14:48.310
Sorry, but you still signed the form.

00:14:48.760 --> 00:14:51.250
You stamped and initialed it, even.

00:14:51.250 --> 00:14:53.700
This might just look like paper to you,

00:14:54.070 --> 00:14:58.370
but in the adult world, 
it's an unbreakable bond.

00:14:58.370 --> 00:15:00.510
Wh-What the...

00:15:00.510 --> 00:15:02.720
There's no cooling-off rule, then?

00:15:03.070 --> 00:15:05.070
We're pros, after all.

00:15:05.420 --> 00:15:07.900
You made a contract with a company.

00:15:07.900 --> 00:15:10.830
That kind of thing can't 
be changed on a whim.

00:15:15.780 --> 00:15:18.750
That means I can't transform 
whenever I want to!

00:15:18.750 --> 00:15:22.340
He said your real form doesn't 
change at all, at least...

00:15:22.340 --> 00:15:24.600
What does he mean, my lifespan's shorter?

00:15:24.600 --> 00:15:25.980
What is this, Horror News?

00:15:26.370 --> 00:15:28.670
Let's quit being magical girls.

00:15:28.670 --> 00:15:30.720
That's destiny anyway.

00:15:31.140 --> 00:15:34.210
Why do you have so much power?

00:15:34.930 --> 00:15:36.990
Your Love Power. Where...

00:15:37.510 --> 00:15:38.670
Well, never mind.

00:15:39.000 --> 00:15:44.070
I guess in five years we've never been close 
enough to know who the other person likes.

00:15:44.070 --> 00:15:44.740
Hey—

00:15:44.740 --> 00:15:45.990
Forget it.

00:15:45.990 --> 00:15:47.820
Just leave me alone.

00:15:49.200 --> 00:15:50.100
Okay.

00:15:56.940 --> 00:15:58.100
Dummy.

00:16:06.660 --> 00:16:08.830
You must have come such a long way!

00:16:09.660 --> 00:16:11.470
Thank you very much!

00:16:22.740 --> 00:16:24.580
We'd better get changed.

00:16:24.580 --> 00:16:25.810
R-Right...

00:16:29.240 --> 00:16:31.190
Quietly...

00:16:32.400 --> 00:16:33.570
I'm here!

00:16:33.570 --> 00:16:36.300
Hey, don't come in the greenroom 
while we're changing!

00:16:36.300 --> 00:16:38.430
But demons are here!

00:16:38.430 --> 00:16:40.940
It's your chance to stand out!

00:16:46.820 --> 00:16:51.550
The fallen angels with severed 
wings now seek rebirth.

00:16:52.020 --> 00:16:54.170
Um...

00:16:54.170 --> 00:16:59.070
the principalities survive their 
jihad and arrive in Elysium.

00:16:59.350 --> 00:17:02.800
The ritual of revival... open the gate!

00:17:04.810 --> 00:17:08.350
PRISMA has arrived!

00:17:08.990 --> 00:17:10.170
Who are they?

00:17:10.170 --> 00:17:11.100
Copycats?

00:17:11.100 --> 00:17:13.360
Forget them! Did you see those monsters?

00:17:13.360 --> 00:17:16.520
Dammit! Be nice to the elderly, 
you whippersnappers!

00:17:16.520 --> 00:17:18.060
Chill.

00:17:20.510 --> 00:17:23.140
Please don't go outside!

00:17:27.360 --> 00:17:29.370
Damn... this is pathetic.

00:17:29.810 --> 00:17:33.370
That I couldn't even look beautiful 
in front of the person I love...

00:17:33.900 --> 00:17:37.440
I admired him from the 
moment I first saw him.

00:17:37.440 --> 00:17:38.570
And that...

00:17:40.320 --> 00:17:43.860
It's giving me a probability-boosting 
chance to hit a major jackpot!

00:17:43.860 --> 00:17:45.840
And yet...

00:17:52.910 --> 00:17:54.930
Michiru!

00:17:57.870 --> 00:18:01.430
Damn... I don't ever get to look cool, do I?

00:18:01.430 --> 00:18:03.370
That's not true.

00:18:03.370 --> 00:18:06.610
Micchi, you've always 
been the ultimate idol.

00:18:10.100 --> 00:18:11.050
PRISMA-san!

00:18:11.510 --> 00:18:14.070
You guys are magical girls, too?

00:18:14.070 --> 00:18:17.130
Saki. We need to focus on that demon.

00:18:17.130 --> 00:18:18.810
Yeah, that's not good...

00:18:19.880 --> 00:18:22.310
We've reached our limits.

00:18:22.310 --> 00:18:25.230
Both as idols and as magical girls...

00:18:25.690 --> 00:18:28.130
Leave useless trash like us alone.

00:18:28.130 --> 00:18:29.200
That's not true!

00:18:29.550 --> 00:18:31.720
You shone so much more brightly before!

00:18:32.960 --> 00:18:36.500
So you can keep shining, 
now, and from now on!

00:18:37.150 --> 00:18:38.760
We can keep shining?

00:18:42.430 --> 00:18:46.880
So don't give up! Reveal your feelings!

00:18:47.060 --> 00:18:48.700
My feelings?

00:18:48.750 --> 00:18:50.270
My feelings?

00:18:56.250 --> 00:18:57.520
I...

00:18:58.370 --> 00:19:00.400
I love...

00:19:00.770 --> 00:19:02.680
Mohiro-chan!

00:19:03.170 --> 00:19:04.710
R-Really?

00:19:05.470 --> 00:19:08.060
I love Saki!

00:19:08.060 --> 00:19:09.640
Who's Saki?

00:19:10.640 --> 00:19:14.680
I... I love Ore-san!

00:19:14.680 --> 00:19:17.550
What? Why am I only just now hearing this?

00:19:17.550 --> 00:19:19.970
I love Michiru!

00:19:19.970 --> 00:19:22.140
Huh? Since when?

00:19:22.140 --> 00:19:24.230
Well, I never told you...

00:19:24.230 --> 00:19:26.960
Um... but...

00:19:27.740 --> 00:19:29.090
Couldn't you tell from my behavior?

00:19:29.090 --> 00:19:31.950
From all my thirsty glances?

00:19:32.340 --> 00:19:34.250
What is with you?

00:19:35.390 --> 00:19:40.270
Does that mean... <i>I'm</i> the 
source of your love power?

00:19:40.270 --> 00:19:42.200
You don't have to say that!

00:19:42.530 --> 00:19:46.030
But let me say it to you straight.

00:19:49.030 --> 00:19:51.660
Michiru. I love you!

00:19:54.010 --> 00:19:57.750
Okay! Now that our hearts 
are in the right place,

00:19:57.750 --> 00:20:00.280
let's beat that demon before 
it gets any bigger!

00:20:03.250 --> 00:20:07.730
Love Power Ultimate Super Dangerous Mode!

00:20:20.760 --> 00:20:22.000
With love...

00:20:22.240 --> 00:20:23.730
With love...

00:20:23.890 --> 00:20:25.360
Through love...

00:20:25.490 --> 00:20:26.860
From love...

00:20:27.330 --> 00:20:29.620
Attack!

00:20:35.560 --> 00:20:38.550
The hell are you doin' in my biz?

00:20:38.550 --> 00:20:42.580
Well... forgive me for 
overstepping my bounds!

00:20:43.110 --> 00:20:49.320
You were runnin' a pretty shady business 
with that borderline illegal contract.

00:20:49.320 --> 00:20:52.570
How are you gonna pay this off, dammit?

00:20:52.570 --> 00:20:54.070
Um, well...

00:20:54.540 --> 00:20:57.550
I admire you so much, Kokoro-san. 
I just wanted to be closer to you!

00:20:57.550 --> 00:21:00.720
Forgive me, Brother! Sorry! Sorry!

00:21:01.360 --> 00:21:03.070
Get your nose off the ground.

00:21:04.260 --> 00:21:05.320
Brother!

00:21:06.150 --> 00:21:07.450
Happy!

00:21:09.760 --> 00:21:12.390
Like hell I'd end it like that!

00:21:26.470 --> 00:21:28.810
Kokoro-chan-san's so scary.

00:21:28.810 --> 00:21:30.840
He's pretty dedicated to
doing the right thing.

00:21:30.840 --> 00:21:32.240
Serves that guy right.

00:21:32.590 --> 00:21:33.480
Hey...

00:21:34.410 --> 00:21:36.940
does that mean I'm gonna 
have to stay like this?

00:21:39.850 --> 00:21:42.670
Stop trying to end the episode with a laugh!

00:21:46.150 --> 00:21:47.980
So now there's more, huh?

00:23:19.960 --> 00:23:34.970
<b>Preview</b>

00:23:26.730 --> 00:23:30.130
<i>Next time, "Magical Girl - Stalking."</i>

00:23:27.720 --> 00:23:34.970
<b>Magical Girl - Stalking</b>

00:23:30.450 --> 00:23:31.670
<i>Next week?</i>

00:23:31.680 --> 00:23:34.180
<i>We don't know what happens that far ahead.</i>

00:23:34.970 --> 00:23:39.980
Illustration: Monokubo
